  "body": "Publishes the independent non-Author product review of #129 at frozen product HEAD `99e40c9af91f9ea36dd3d4ba97eccad46f6c6e14`.\n\n**\u9650\u5b9aI5\u72ec\u7acb\u30ec\u30d3\u30e5\u30fcPASS \u2014 bounded I5 typed admission only. Product defects: 0. Unresolved findings: 3 Medium boundary findings (I5-A1, I5-B1, I5-C1) deferred to I6 Wire; 2 Low observation findings verified/mitigated (I5-D1, I5-F1); 2 open carryovers (I4-E1 Low, Task G G-R1 Medium). Whole-product/whole-ADR acceptance remains NOT READY.**\n\nRead the [independent report](https://github.com/TakashiSasaki/git-repo-db/blob/b4ede5d8a87f3ce7b1f6df8fda5b3051c3865ba2/docs/implementation/evidence/adr0031-i5/independent/REPORT.md), [evidence and reproduction guide](https://github.com/TakashiSasaki/git-repo-db/blob/b4ede5d8a87f3ce7b1f6df8fda5b3051c3865ba2/docs/implementation/evidence/adr0031-i5/independent/README.md), [machine summary](https://github.com/TakashiSasaki/git-repo-db/blob/b4ede5d8a87f3ce7b1f6df8fda5b3051c3865ba2/docs/implementation/evidence/adr0031-i5/independent/summary.json), [findings register](https://github.com/TakashiSasaki/git-repo-db/blob/b4ede5d8a87f3ce7b1f6df8fda5b3051c3865ba2/docs/implementation/evidence/adr0031-i5/independent/findings.json), and [all-79 first-failure comparison](https://github.com/TakashiSasaki/git-repo-db/blob/b4ede5d8a87f3ce7b1f6df8fda5b3051c3865ba2/docs/implementation/evidence/adr0031-i5/independent/failure-classification.json).\n\nThis PR adds **11 independent-review evidence files only**. All existing base entries retain their exact Git blobs. Product code, tests, DDL/UDF/fingerprints, accepted decisions, and original Author evidence are unchanged. PR #129 and its branch remain unchanged. The report and ZIP are frozen records of the completed review; publishing evidence does not claim a new product execution at this publication commit.\n\n| Independently executed per actual SQLite engine | 3.51.3 | 3.53.1 |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| Reviewer-designed counterexamples | 15/15 pass | 15/15 pass |\n| I5 focused pytest | 29/29 pass | 29/29 pass |\n| I4 focused pytest | 217/217 pass | 217/217 pass |\n| Existing I3 subset within broad regression | 65/65 pass | 65/65 pass |\n| Original SQL diagnostic groups | 301/301 pass | 301/301 pass |\n| Original corruption nodes plus restoration observer | 8/8 pass | 8/8 pass |\n| Broad regression, exit **1** | 3,058 pass / 59 call failures / 20 setup errors | Same |\n\nAll **79 final I4 non-success node/phase/refusal positions remain**: 45 Transfer call failures, 20 Transfer setup errors, 14 I6 Wire call failures. **Zero added, zero resolved.** All failure nodes, phases, and refusal exceptions match the baseline with 100% fidelity. No skip/xfail or assertion reduction earns acceptance; later assertions and 2,541 ordinary nodes remain unexecuted.\n\nFresh direct and sdist-derived wheels were installed outside checkout and actually run on both engines. **All four combinations pass 29/29 I5, 217/217 I4, and 15/15 independent counterexample cases**, with installed file hashes matching the source. Original I2/I3 distribution probes pass. All four original Access smokes still exit **1** at Transfer preflight; distribution orchestration exits **1**. Runtime source IDs, compile options, PRAGMAs, deterministic UDF flags, and DDL fingerprints are retained.\n\n### Focus Findings (Points A\u2013F)\n- **I5-A1 (Medium)**: Store admission lacks caller authorization checks; untrusted caller authorization deferred to I6 Wire / Selective Exchange.\n- **I5-B1 (Medium)**: Implicit parent evidence completion synthesizes event clock and causes false dependency failure; explicit parent reports mandatory for I6 Wire.\n- **I5-C1 (Medium)**: Endpoint declaration auto-synthesis masks wire truncation, admitting truncated events as genuine 1-sided transfers; explicit declared endpoints mandatory for I6 Wire.\n- **I5-D1 (Low)**: Author atomicity test tested pre-flight check rather than SQL rollback; verified **PASS** via independent counterexample injecting in-flight trigger failure on second endpoint (`ROLLBACK TO p1_transfer_event` leaves 0 partial writes).\n- **I5-F1 (Low)**: `has_transfer_fence()` inspects only one trigger; mitigated by `Context._validate_schema()` checking full schema against `expected_schema('context')`.\n- **I4-E1 (Low, Carryover)**: Sdist input scope differs between Author execution and public tree due to post-execution evidence additions.\n- **Task G G-R1 (Medium, Carryover)**: Context candidate identity scoping deferred to ADR 0031 I7.\n\nExact bindings:\n- Base #128: `2003a9ee4f25907bcf96a634980b8caffc133c4e`, tree `7a662517644541c3c321a111b9325e97ea5667a8`.\n- Author execution: `3a749541fe4c41eb72e7ded9f36528f0abeb05ff`, tree `6a494efb510713dbfb3cebf6ef5ff85e703e0d18`.\n- Reviewed public product / independent execution / this PR's parent: `99e40c9af91f9ea36dd3d4ba97eccad46f6c6e14`, tree `d2d69b3094c8e07e375fc357e979ed8131bf39c5`.\n- **Review publication HEAD: `b4ede5d8a87f3ce7b1f6df8fda5b3051c3865ba2`; tree: `c7d3aabb2063a24bc9057951c80f8cc865c660f8`.**\n- Independent ZIP: **1,757,961 bytes**, SHA-256 `a8208c0cdb61ba7df1e59195af2c2e5005c34fbeb96e1f4ff3ff9513f866a0c9`; **124 indexed payload entries**, all reverified for publication.\n- Author ZIP's bytes/hash (3,305,637 bytes, SHA-256 `c83f97e6276ad9134adee02f7f73fd0af2df49db32414410a502e049aaf67f9b`) and all 138 entries independently verified against `artifact-index.json`.\n\nBoth product Transfer fences remain active. I6 Wire admission, I7 Recovery reconciliation (including Task G G-R1), and I8 Query/Search remain separate mandatory obligations before Transfer operations can be integrated.\n\nDedicated branch, Draft PR stacked on PR #129; no merge, release, deployment, P8, or real Provider/catalog operation.\n",
